      "content": "While the tax code structure is a significant contributing factor, the issue is deeply intertwined with specific political decisions. Tax cuts disproportionately favoring corporations and high-net-worth individuals have directly increased the share of total income going to the top. Furthermore, deregulation in finance and other sectors has often led to increased earning potential for those already in positions of power, widening the wealth gap. These policy choices create a self-reinforcing cycle where capital accumulates faster than labor income.",
