      "content": "It suggests that current policies tend to favor the accumulation and retention of existing wealth. In this cycle, wealth generates more wealth through investments, outpacing wage growth for the majority. While modest adjustments can help, many economists argue that rectifying deep structural inequality requires significant interventions like progressive taxation, stronger labor protections, and investments in public goods. These radical shifts aim to rebalance economic power away from pure capital accumulation toward broader societal equity.",
